  "learn": {
    "title": "One Press, One Count",
    "body": "Wire the button between D2 and GND and enable INPUT_PULLUP: pressed reads LOW. Wire D9 → 220 Ω → LED anode, with the cathode to GND.\n\nKeep a raw reading, a stable reading and the time of the last raw change. Accept a new stable state only after 30 ms without a change. Increment only on the stable HIGH-to-LOW edge; a held LOW is not another press. Toggle the LED for each accepted press and print COUNT=1, COUNT=2, and so on.\n\nRun, press and hold for at least half a second, release for at least 100 ms, then press and hold again. The first press lights the LED; the second turns it off. Rapid transitions shorter than 30 ms must not add counts. Use millis(), so the loop can keep observing the button.",
    "links": []
  },
